// ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ DEMO MAIN ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ {


// ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ INPUT ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ {

// --- DEMO PARAMS INPUTS ---{
i_s1 = input.text_area(
						  "aaa\nbb\nc"
						  , "S1", group="Sample strings" )
i_s2 = input.text_area(
						  "QQQQQ\nRRRR\nSSS\nTT"
						  , "S2", group="Sample strings")

const string IG_WRAP = "Wrap and concatenation parameters"
i_wrapTo 			= input.int	  	(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "1", defval = 80, title = "Wrap to")
i_separator 		= input.string	(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "1", defval = "", title=  "Separator", tooltip = "'\\n' can be used for line break")
iSeparator = i_separator == "" ? "" : str.replace_all(i_separator, "\\n", "\n")
i_wrapPrefix		= input.string	(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "p", defval = "", title = "Wrap: prefix"			, tooltip = "Added before separator")
i_wrapPostfix		= input.string	(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "p", defval = "", title = "postfix"				, tooltip = "Added after separator")
i_wrapLinePostfix	= input.string	(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "p", defval = "", title = "line postfix"			, tooltip = "Added after every wrapped line (if wrapped) (not after new line breaks, but after original).")
iWrapLinePostfix = i_wrapLinePostfix == "" ? "" : str.replace_all(i_wrapLinePostfix, "\\n", "\n")

sWrapParams = str.format( "Wrap params: 
						  \nWrap to: {0}	
						  \nSeparator: {1}	
						  \nPrefix: {2}	
						  \nPostfix: {3}	
						  \nLine postfix: {4}	
						  "
						  , i_wrapTo
						  , i_separator
						  , i_wrapPrefix
						  , i_wrapPostfix
						  , i_wrapLinePostfix
						  )




const string IG_PRINT = "Print parameters"
i_printLineNumbers				= input.bool	(group = IG_PRINT, inline = "n", defval = false				, title =  "Print line numbers")
i_printLineNumberFormat			= input.string	(group = IG_PRINT, inline = "n", defval = "L{0,number,0000}: "		, title =  "Line number format")
i_printPrintToLastLine			= input.bool	(group = IG_PRINT, inline = "ll", defval = false				, title =  "Print to last line")


sPrintParams = str.format( "Print params:
						  \nPrint line numbers: {0}	
						  \nLine number format: \"{1}\"	
						  \nPrint to last line: {2} 	
						  "
						  , i_printLineNumbers ? "true" : "false"
						  , i_printLineNumberFormat
						  , i_printPrintToLastLine ? "true" : "false"
						  )

i_maxL				= input.int		(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "L", defval = 1000		, title =  "Max length")
i_maxLn				= input.int		(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "L", defval = 1000		, title =  "Max lines" )
i_truncLeft			= input.string	(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "t", defval = "Left"		, title =  "Truncate", options=["Left", "Right"])
i_truncTop			= input.string	(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "t", defval = "Bottom"	, title =  "", options=["Bottom", "Top"])
i_truncSrc			= input.bool	(group = IG_WRAP, inline = "t", defval = true		, title =  "orig string",  tooltip="if one of the args is already above limit - truncate it")
iTruncateLeft		= i_truncLeft ==				 "Left" ? true : false
iTruncateTop		= i_truncTop ==				 "Top" ? true : false

sTruncParams = str.format( "Truncate params:
						  \nMax length: {0}	
						  \nMax lines: {1}	
						  \nTruncate: {2} and {3}	
						  \nTruncate source: {4}	
						  "
						  , i_maxL			
						  , i_maxLn			
						  , i_truncLeft		
						  , i_truncTop		
						  , i_truncSrc		
						  )



// END OF DEMO PARAMS INPUTS }

// --- TABLE INPUTS ---{
i_tblH =  input.int(group="Table properties", defval = 100, title = "Table height", inline = "")
i_tblHeadersH =  input.int(group="Table properties", defval = 10, title = "Rows height: header rows", inline = "rows")
i_tblParamRow1H =  input.int(group="Table properties", defval = 10, title = "Param row1", inline = "rows1")
i_tblParamRow2H =  input.int(group="Table properties", defval = 20, title = "Params row2", inline = "rows1")
i_tblOutputRowH =  input.int(group="Table properties", defval = 70, title = "Output", inline = "rows")
i_col0W = input.int(group="Table properties", defval = 60, title = "Column width: left", inline = "w")
i_col1W = input.int(group="Table properties", defval = 40, title = "right", inline = "w")

totalHeight = i_tblHeadersH + i_tblParamRow1H + i_tblParamRow2H + i_tblOutputRowH
iRow0H = i_tblH * i_tblHeadersH 	/ totalHeight /2
iRow1H = i_tblH * i_tblHeadersH 	/ totalHeight /2
iRow2H = i_tblH * i_tblParamRow1H 	/ totalHeight 
iRow3H = i_tblH * i_tblParamRow2H 	/ totalHeight 
iRow4H = i_tblH * i_tblOutputRowH 	/ totalHeight

totalWidth = i_col0W + i_col1W
iCol0W = 100 * (i_col0W / totalWidth)
iCol1W = 100 * (i_col1W / totalWidth)
iCell0Wsmaller = iCol0W / 3 
// --- input lblSize --- {
i_textSize        = input.string  (group = "text", inline = "lbls1", defval = "Small", title="Size", options= ["Auto", "Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"])

//Turn the input into a proper label size value
simple string iTextSize =   switch i_textSize
	"Auto"    => size.auto  	
	"Tiny"    => size.tiny  
	"Small"   => size.small 
	"Normal"  => size.normal
	"Large"   => size.large 
	"Huge"    => size.huge  
	=> size.normal

// END OF lblSize input }

const string IG_SCROLL = "Scroll output"
i_scrollEnable	 			= input.bool	(group=IG_SCROLL, inline = "sc1", defval = true , title = "Enable scroll")
i_scrollShowLineNumbers 	= input.bool	(group=IG_SCROLL, inline = "sc1", defval = false, title = "Line #'s")
i_scrollStartLine	 		= input.int		(group=IG_SCROLL, inline = "sc", defval = 1 , title = "Start line")
i_scrollWindowLines 		= input.int		(group=IG_SCROLL, inline = "sc", defval = 30, title = "Scroll window height, lines")




//}


// ▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲ END OF INPUT  ▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲ }


var t = table.new(position.bottom_center, 4, 5, bgcolor = color.rgb(245, 243, 149), border_color = color.black, border_width = 1, frame_color = color.black, frame_width = 1)
if barstate.islastconfirmedhistory

	// init var for cell 0,0 of the table 
	txtOut0 = ""
	txtOut1 = ""

	// ━━━━━ test print() ━━━━━{
	txtOut0 += "\n\n -------- TEST print() -------- \n\n"
	txtOut0 += "Prints S1 to S2\n"
	txtOut0 += i_s2.print(i_s1, i_maxL, i_maxLn, iTruncateLeft, iTruncateTop, i_truncSrc, i_printLineNumbers, i_printLineNumberFormat, i_printPrintToLastLine)
	//}

	// ━━━━━ test concatTrunc() ━━━━━{
	txtOut0 += "\n\n -------- TEST concatTrunc() -------- \n\n"
	txtOut0 += "\n\n Concatenate \n\n"
	txtOut0 += str.format("concatTrunc(S2, S1, ...): \n{0}", i_s2.concatTrunc(i_s1, iSeparator, i_maxL, iTruncateLeft))
	//}

	// ━━━━━ test concatTrunc2() ━━━━━{
	txtOut0 += "\n\n -------- TEST concatTrunc2() -------- \n\n"
	[cc, bb] = concatTrunc2(i_s2, i_s1, iSeparator, i_maxL, iTruncateLeft)
	txtOut0 += str.format("concatTrunc2(S2, S1, ...) truncate to {2} chars:  \n{0}\nTruncated {1} chars.", cc, bb, i_maxL) 
	//}

	// ━━━━━ test wrap() ━━━━━ {

	// --- create and wrap a long string --- {

	// CREATE 
	// Let's make a string of 4084 chars (pinescript limit = 4096 chars) and 
	// wrap it to the width of e.g. 100 chars, which will add at least 40 separator strings (together with prefixes if any)
	// which will make the string at least 4084 + 40 = 4124 chars long, which is above limit, 
	// so truncation will be required
	txtWrapOneLongLine = ""
	for j = 0 to 408
		txtWrapOneLongLine += "123456789_"
	txtWrapOneLongLine+="ABCD"
	// log.info("\nINIT STRINGS:\ntxtWrapOneLongLine length = {0}", str.length(txtWrapOneLongLine))

	// WRAP!
	// txtWrapOneLongLine := txtWrapOneLongLine.wrap(i_wrapTo,"-...","...-")
	//}

	// --- create and wrap a long multiline string ---{ 
	// of 4080 chars (pinescript limit = 4096 chars)
	// wrapping to the width of e.g. 100 chars will add at least 40 separator strings (together with prefixes if any)
	// which will make the string at least 4084 + 40 = 4124 chars long, which is above limit, 
	// so truncation will be required

	// CREATE 
	// 19 lines of 206 chars (including "\n") each  starting with line number "L01: " = 3914 chars  
	txtWrapMultilineLongLine = ""
	for j = 0 to 17 // 19 * 206 chars 
		txtWrapMultilineLongLine += str.format("L{0, number, 00}: ", j) // 5 chars
		for k = 1 to 20 // 200 chars
			txtWrapMultilineLongLine += "123456789_"
		txtWrapMultilineLongLine += "\n" // 1 char
	
 	// add one more line of 176 chars to bring the text length to 4090 chars 
	txtWrapMultilineLongLine += "L18: " 
	for k = 1 to 16 
		txtWrapMultilineLongLine +=  "123456789_"
	// log.info("\nINIT STRINGS:\ntxtWrapOneLongLine length = {0}", str.length(txtWrapOneLongLine))

	// WRAP
	txtWrapMultilineLongLineOrig = txtWrapMultilineLongLine
	txtWrapMultilineLongLine := txtWrapMultilineLongLine.wrap(i_wrapTo,i_wrapPrefix,i_wrapPostfix, iWrapLinePostfix)
	f = str.substring(txtWrapMultilineLongLine, 0,1) == "\n"
	// log.info("\ntxtWrapMultilineLongLine length = {0}", str.length(txtWrapMultilineLongLine))

	txtOut1 := txtWrapMultilineLongLine
	//}

	// ^^^ END OF test wrap() } 


	// ━━━━━ draw table ━━━━━ {
	// TEST ALL 
	const color BG_COLOR = color.rgb(245, 243, 149)

	// --- ADD CELLS AND MERGE --- {
	table.cell(t,0,0, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow0H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,1,0, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow0H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,2,0, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow0H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,3,0, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCol1W		 , 	height = iRow0H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,0,1, text_halign = text.align_center, text_valign = text.align_top,width = iCell0Wsmaller,	height = iRow1H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,1,1, text_halign = text.align_center, text_valign = text.align_top,width = iCell0Wsmaller,	height = iRow1H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,2,1, text_halign = text.align_center, text_valign = text.align_top,width = iCell0Wsmaller,	height = iRow1H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,3,1, text_halign = text.align_center, text_valign = text.align_top,width = iCol1W		  ,	height = iRow1H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,0,2, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow2H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,1,2, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow2H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,2,2, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow2H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,3,2, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCol1W		 , 	height = iRow2H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,0,3, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow3H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,1,3, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow3H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,2,3, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow3H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,3,3, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCol1W		 , 	height = iRow3H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,0,4, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow4H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,1,4, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow4H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,2,4, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCell0Wsmaller, 	height = iRow4H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,3,4, text_halign = text.align_left, text_valign = text.align_top, width = iCol1W		 , 	height = iRow4H, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)

	// merge first 3 cells in header rows
	table.merge_cells(t, 0,0,2,0)
	table.merge_cells(t, 0,1,2,1)

	// merge first 3 cells in output row
	table.merge_cells(t, 0,4,2,4)

	// merge last column cells
	table.merge_cells(t, 3,0,3,4)

	//}

	// --- POPULATE HEADERS --- {

	// --- 1st row -- 
	// ---- CELL(0,0) --- 
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 0, 0, "")
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 0, 0, text_size = size.normal)
	table.cell_set_bgcolor		(t, 0, 0,BG_COLOR)

	// --- 2nd row --- 
	// ---- CELL(0,1) --- 
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 0, 1, "TEST STRINGLIB FUNCTIONS")
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 0, 1, text_size = size.normal)
	table.cell_set_bgcolor		(t, 0, 1,color.rgb(236, 197, 4))
	//}

	// --- POPULATE PARAMS --- {
	// --- 3nd row --- 

	// ---- CELL(*,2) --- 
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 0, 2, "PARAM S1:\n---\n" +  i_s1)
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 0, 2, iTextSize)
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 1, 2, "PARAM S2:\n---\n" +  i_s2)
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 1, 2, iTextSize)
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 2, 2, "")
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 2, 2, "PARAM S2:\n---\n" + sPrintParams)
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 2, 2, iTextSize)

	// ---- CELL(*,3) --- 
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 0, 3, "PARAM\n---\n" + sWrapParams)
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 0, 3, iTextSize)
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 1, 3, "PARAM\n---\n" + sTruncParams)
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 1, 3, iTextSize)
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 2, 3, "Latest close:" + "")
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 2, 3, iTextSize)
	//}
	
	// ---- POPULATE OUTPUT CELLS ---{

	// ---- CELL(0,4) --- 
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 3, 0, txtOut0)
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 3, 0, iTextSize)
	if i_scrollEnable
		txtOut1 := txtOut1.scroll(i_scrollStartLine, i_scrollWindowLines, i_scrollShowLineNumbers)
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 0, 4, "TEST scroll():\n---\n" + txtOut1)
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 0, 4, iTextSize)
	//}

	// END OF DRAW TABLE} 

	

if barstate.islast
	// ---- CELL(1,2) --- 
	varip scrollingClose = ""
	scrollingClose := scrollingClose.print(str.tostring(close), max_lines = i_maxLn, truncate_top = true, truncate_lines_src = true)
	table.cell_set_text			(t, 2, 3, str.format("TEST print():\n---\nLastest close - {0} lines:\n{1}", i_maxLn, scrollingClose))
	table.cell_set_text_size	(t, 2, 3, iTextSize)


// ▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲ END OF DEMO MAIN  ▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲▲ }

